Hi Alex,

As promised on the call, here is the IT side in writing. I've split it into decisions
that are still ours to make and things we honestly can't answer.

Still ours to decide or provide (we'll come back to you on each):

- Dynamics 365 sandbox: you'll need a Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations sandbox for
  development and testing. We haven't ordered it yet and we haven't decided whether it
  will be a dedicated sandbox or shared with our finance upgrade project. That's our
  call; I'll confirm which, and when it's available.
- Integration method: not decided yet. Our D365 partner prefers the standard data
  entities over OData, but our architects are also considering file-based batch
  integration through the data management framework. We'll tell you which one.
- Single sign-on: your system must use single sign-on. We're in the middle of moving
  from Okta to Microsoft Entra ID and haven't decided whether the automation goes on
  Entra from day one. IT security decides that this quarter.
- Network: we will provide the network for the automation, but we haven't yet decided
  whether it gets its own VLAN or shares the warehouse VLAN. We need your network
  requirements first.

What we cannot tell you:

- The legacy WMS. It was built in-house in 2009 by a contractor who left in 2015.
  There is no documentation, no interface list and no test environment. Over the
  years interfaces were added to label printers, the old conveyor, a returns tool,
  carrier manifests and several Excel macros that read its database directly.
- We genuinely do not know how many interfaces there are or what format each one
  uses. Our best guess is "between eight and twenty", but that is a guess. Nobody,
  including us, will know until your team traces them in the code and the database
  during the migration.
- We don't want this to hold up the proposal, and we can't remove the uncertainty
  for you. Please carry an allowance for the unknown interfaces in your price rather
  than assume the low end.

Regards,
